{
  "summary": "Introduces a named constant `Sock::MAX_WAIT_TIMEOUT` (in whole seconds, equivalent to `INT_MAX / 1000`) for the socket wait timeout cap introduced in PR 36340, and documents this cap in the Doxygen comments for `Sock::Wait()` and `WaitMany()`. In `bitcoin-cli`, it replaces the 5-year timeout placeholder for `-rpcclienttimeout=0` with `Sock::MAX_WAIT_TIMEOUT` and updates CLI help text to explain that 0 selects the maximum supported timeout (about 24 days).",
  "problem": "PR 36340 capped socket wait times using an inline calculation in `Sock::WaitMany`, leaving the maximum timeout undocumented in `Sock` headers. Additionally, `bitcoin-cli` documented `-rpcclienttimeout=0` as \"no timeout\" and implemented it via an arbitrary 5-year duration that was already being implicitly truncated to ~24.8 days by socket wait loops.",
